## 💥 The Problem

Modern software teams spend nearly **30% of their day context-switching** between disjointed tools:
* Code diffs live on **GitHub**.
* Requirements and specs live in **Linear/Jira**.
* Clarifications and reviewer debates vanish into ephemeral **Slack/Discord threads**.

This friction leads to stale pull requests, outdated tickets, missed breaking changes, and delayed deployment cycles.

---

## ⚡ The Solution: Crux

Crux collapses the fragmented review and triage loop into a high-density, real-time command center:
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                  CRUX COCKPIT                                     |
+----------------------+----------------------------+-------------------------------+
|  1. METADATA & TASKS |   2. LIVE DIFF & CODE      |     3. REAL-TIME THREADS      |
|                      |                            |                               |
|  • Linked Issues     |  • Real-time Diff Viewer   |  • Multiplayer Live Presence  |
|  • CI/CD Health      |  • AI Reviewer Brief       |  • Markdown & Code Blocks     |
|  • Assignees/Status  |  • Breaking Schema Alerts  |  • One-click Sync to PR       |
+----------------------+----------------------------+-------------------------------+

## 🚀 Core Features

### 1. 🖥️ Unified 3-Column Cockpit
* **Left Column (Context):** View active issue specs, Linear/GitHub metadata, commit histories, and deployment statuses at a glance.
* **Center Column (Code & AI Briefs):** Clean, syntax-highlighted PR diffs augmented with automated impact summaries.
* **Right Column (Multiplayer Discussion):** Low-latency, multi-user real-time chat with presence awareness—never lose code review context in general Slack channels again.

### 2. 🧠 AI Reviewer Briefs
* **Critical Path Extraction:** Highlights which modules carry production risk before you read line-by-line.
* **Schema Drift Alerts:** Automatically detects database migrations, breaking API contracts, and mutated interfaces.
* **Test Coverage Gap Analysis:** Pinpoints un-tested edge cases introduced in the branch.

### 3. 🧪 Zero-Friction Sandbox Mode
* Instant, one-click guest access preloaded with realistic sample repos and live mocks.
* Enables hackathon judges and prospective teams to experience multiplayer live synchronization without configuring GitHub OAuth tokens upfront.

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

* **Frontend:** React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Lucide Icons
* **Real-time Engine:** WebSockets / Supabase Realtime / Liveblocks
* **Syntax & Diffs:** Monaco Editor / PrismJS / Diff2Html
* **AI Analysis:** LLM pipeline structured for AST-aware diff summarization
* **Deployment:** Vercel

